correction, the part about numCs and numTs, I was wrong. I got confused by the column names. The default text file format has freqC and freqT for those column names and they are percent methylation values. So your file format is correct. But as I said you are losing the region boundary information by reading the file that way, and I think the promoter boundaries are not correct in your attached file.

Best,
Altuna

