MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

it seems you are taking the 3' end as well, you can see in your tracks that they overlap with 3' ends of transcripts.

gene.obj=read.transcript.features("/users/GD/resource/mouse/mm9/annotation/genes/UCSC_annotation.bed", up.flank=1050, down.flank=1050)

gene.obj is a list of GRanges objects that have promoter locations defined by up.flank and down.flank, assume "methylRawList.obj" is a set of CpGs (base-pairs) you read in into R.

regional.methylRaw=regionCounts(methylRawList.obj, gene.obj$promoters)

then you can do unite() and do the differential methylation test.

I hope it is more clear now
Best,
Altuna

