methylKitR_promoter.txt  file is the promoters defined by methylKit. Here please grep "-913" entry in the file. One observation for chrM is having -ve position. Please explain is that possible? I am also attaching the gene annotation files so that you can calculate the boundaries from tss.

ii) I matched promoters from methylKit and my file. I found 20991 entries match (14421 uniq as there are same promoters for different transcripts : matched_promoters), but other promoters either matched half or didn't match at all.
                                       METHYLKIT                                MY PROMOTER                     Overlap               TSS
e.g. at one position:
                               chr1    4846774    4847874      +    chr1    4847408    4848508      +        466                    4848408 (as per my UCSC file)

Similarly for other entries too. Now there could be two possibilities: i) TSS is different in the two file formats ii) Either one of us is calculating it in a wrong way. I have checked in my file for some entries and I found them correct according to the position of TSS. I may be wrong. That's why I am attaching following files:
i) mm9 annotation input methylkit
ii) mm9 annotation file I used for promoters extraction (which includes TSS position as well with "txStart" header)
iii) matched promoter entries in both of us analysis
iv) promoters I exported from methylKit
v) My promoter list

I request you to kindly look in the files for some errors. And why is there -ve entries in the file?
I suppose that for annotation information, these are the only files which is required, so that you can re-run the annotation and export the files, in case I am wrong.
I would highly appreciate your reply,

Shalu

